Aim: Automate the process of running containerized application developed in exercise 7 using Kubernetes

Implementation and outputs:
Step 1: Verify the current deployment
Command 1: kubectl get deployments

Command 2: kubectl get pods

Step 2: Scale to three replicas
Command 3: kubectl scale deployment student-api --replicas=3

Command 4: kubectl get pods
Three Student API pods are created and reach Running.

Step 3: Demonstrate self-healing
Copy the name of one Student API pod:
Command 5: kubectl get pods

Delete that specific pod:
Command 6: kubectl delete pod YOUR_POD_NAME

Check again:
Command 7: kubectl get pods
Kubernetes should create a replacement pod to maintain the desired replica count.

Step 4: Restart the Deployment
Command 8: kubectl rollout restart deployment student-api

Command 9: kubectl rollout status deployment student-api
Check whether the link is working or not
http://localhost:30080/students

Step 5: Restore one replica
Command 10: kubectl scale deployment student-api --replicas=1

Command 11: kubectl get pods
Wait until the terminating pods disappear and one pod remains Running.
